<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CallerAPI live voice filter for ConnexCS, as a ConneXML app.

  ConnexCS forks the call audio to CallerAPI while the call runs. CallerAPI
  transcribes it, runs the scam rules on every line, runs the model when
  the rules cannot phrase it, and posts a verdict to your Falcon the moment
  the score changes. Falcon ties the verdict to the INVITE it screened,
  shows it in the dashboard, pages your webhook, and blocks the next call
  from that number. Nobody touches the live call.

  Setup:
  1. Class 5 > Apps > + > ConneXML. Paste this file.
  2. Replace YOUR_CALLERAPI_KEY and falcon.example.com.
  3. Route the calls you want listened to through this app. Start with one
     route or a sampled share. Every call through here is a Class 5 call
     on ConnexCS and a metered minute on CallerAPI.
  4. report=true files a confirmed scam caller into the CallerAPI spam
     database at the end of the call. Start with report=false.

  Confirm with ConnexCS support before go-live, the docs do not state them:
  - The audio format on the socket. CallerAPI accepts Twilio style JSON
    frames, its own JSON start line, or bare mu-law or PCM16 frames. Bare
    frames take call_id and from from the URL, so both are set twice below.
  - The variable names for the caller, the destination, and the call id in
    ConneXML. {{ cli }}, {{ dest }}, and {{ call_id }} are placeholders.
-->
<Response>
  <Start>
    <Stream url="wss://api.callerapi.com/api/voice/filter/stream?key=YOUR_CALLERAPI_KEY&amp;webhook=https://falcon.example.com/v1/voice/verdict&amp;report=false&amp;call_id={{ call_id }}&amp;from={{ cli }}" mix_type="mixed">
      <Parameter name="call_id" value="{{ call_id }}" />
      <Parameter name="from" value="{{ cli }}" />
    </Stream>
  </Start>
  <Dial>{{ dest }}</Dial>
</Response>
